- \`/replica-deploy\` - Preflight, production services, domain, monitoring. Use it: Last stage.
- \`/skill-authoring\` - Write a skill, an agent instruction file, or a rules document another agent reads. Use it: When the user asks for one.
- \`/setup-template\` - Judge each element - present, working, old shape gone - and prove it with the real thing. Use it: When the user asks whether a setup or migration is finished.

When a request matches one of these skills and the user has not typed its command, say which command applies and ask for it in one line rather than guessing at the contents. When the user types the command, follow the instructions that arrive with their message - they are the skill, and they replace your own approach to that kind of work.
</skills>
